      "math_academy_id": "q-33977",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨4,1,6⟩+t⟨2,6,0⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩=-32.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨4+2t,1+6t,6⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨4+2t,1+6t,6⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =-32 \\\\ ⟨4+2t,1+6t,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =-32 \\\\ -24(4+2t)+8(1+6t)+6\\cdot 6 & =-32 \\\\ -96-48t+8+48t+36 & =-32 \\\\ -52 & =-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect.",
